exfat_get_blk_dev_info() refuses to run unless the release uname() reports
is at least 2.6, the kernel version from which on the /sys/dev/block
attributes it reads exist.  On LikeOS that release is the LikeOS version
("0.2.9"), which would refuse every device; LikeOS provides those
attributes (start, partition, removable, device, slaves, alignment_offset),
so the version test is skipped.

